<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TestCaseEntity>
   <description>Mirrors Jira US-02 / PT-197 (App-Switch Navigation Control, Done) using the account from PT-272's repro steps, confirmed 6/17/2026 to exist in both SE and SS with working switch behavior. PT-272 (open, Blocked on tracing infra, not a functional blocker) documents switching as slow — ~2-3s SS->SE, ~2s SE->SS — hence the 20s element waits. Requires VPN/Tailscale; login selectors verified live 9/21/2026, app-switch tab selectors verified live via Object Spy 9/23/2026. Updated 10/1/2026 now that the 2FA blocker is resolved: login actually reaches a &quot;Switch Company&quot; account-switcher step (inside an iframe) that every prior run was blocked from seeing. This account has multiple companies — the test now loops through all of them via the `Data Files/SupplierCompanies` data file, confirming app-switch works the same for each. Notes from the first full pass (10/1/2026): (1) the SE/SS app switcher is collapsed behind an arrow tab and must be hovered open before clicking; (2) both apps render inside the same shell iframe, so content is checked via captured objects (`div_Recent Activity`, `div_Onboarding Suppliers`) rather than page-text search; (3) the SCiEnable heading reads &quot;Onboarding Suppliers&quot; for gpm.scienable vs &quot;Onboarding Checklist&quot; per PT-268 — the object matches structurally so either passes; (4) switching SE -&gt; SS lands on the Switch Company screen instead of the SS home the user left — the test re-selects the company and logs a report warning (possible defect, pending confirmation with Lejla/dev); (5) the next-company step uses enhancedClick on &quot;Switch Company&quot; because the header hover menu doesn't reliably open after the app switcher has been used. The &quot;Invalid login credentials&quot; check only searches the outer page, so it is weak coverage for FR-7.</description>
   <name>TC_AppSwitch_NavigateBetweenSEandSS</name>
